  "result": "Done! I've implemented the overdue report functionality:\n\n**Added `overdueInvoices(invoices, asOf)` in src/reports.js:**\n- Returns array of overdue invoices sorted by most overdue first\n- **Each overdue invoice includes:** { number, customerId, dueDate, daysOverdue, due }\n- **Filter criteria:**\n  - Status must be 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid invoices)\n  - dueDate must be strictly before asOf (not including the same day)\n- **Sorting:** By daysOverdue descending (most overdue first)\n- **Calculations:**\n  - daysOverdue: using daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)\n  - due: using balanceDue(invoice) to account for payments\n- No validation required; returns empty array if no invoices are overdue\n\n**Added 17 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty invoice list\n- No overdue invoices\n- Invoices overdue by various amounts\n- Invoice due today (not included in report)\n- Invoice due tomorrow (not included)\n- Status filtering (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- Sorting by daysOverdue (most overdue first)\n- Correct daysOverdue calculation\n- Correct due amount calculation\n- Multiple customers\n- Input array non-mutation\n- EOM payment terms\n- Large overdue amounts\n- Edge cases\n\nAll 221 tests pass \u2713 (204 existing + 17 new report tests)",
